   \end{comment}
			Recalling that $\epsilon:=\frac{r-q}{2}$, this consequently yields:
			\[q<s_{j+1}^a\leq s_{j}^a + \epsilon \leq q +\epsilon <r\]
			proving the lemma, i.e.\  $\exists s\in Q_+$ such that $q<s^a<r$.\end{proof}

